wine-bleeding-wb-build — recommended build dependencies metapackage
==================================================================

This metapackage declares Recommends: on the tools needed to build Wine
components (DXVK, VKD3D-Proton, DXVK-NVAPI) and Wine itself from source
using the wb Component Builder and Build Dist from Source dialogs.

Installing this package pulls in what your distro provides. Any tool not
available in your distro's repositories can be built from source: wb-gui
runs wb-preflight at startup and offers per-tool "Build from source"
buttons for glslang, MinGW-w64, and meson.

Quick start
-----------

    dnf install wine-bleeding-wb-build   # Fedora / RHEL + EPEL
    zypper install wine-bleeding-wb-build # openSUSE

Then launch wb-gui and open Component Builder or Build Dist from Source.
The preflight dialog will list any remaining gaps with actionable fixes.

Tools covered
-------------

  gcc, gcc-c++          C / C++ compiler (Wine host build)
  make                  Build orchestration
  meson                 Build system (DXVK, VKD3D-Proton, DXVK-NVAPI)
  ninja-build           Build backend for meson
  glslang               GLSL→SPIR-V compiler (DXVK shaders)
  mingw64-gcc           MinGW-w64 cross-compiler (Windows PE targets)
  mingw64-gcc-c++       MinGW-w64 C++ cross-compiler
  pkgconf-pkg-config    Package metadata queries
  git                   Source tree management
  flex, bison           Wine configure prerequisites (dist build only)
  autoconf              Wine configure prerequisites (dist build only)

Package names above are Fedora conventions. Other distros use equivalent
packages; wb-preflight shows the distro-specific install command at runtime.

Managed build-tools
-------------------

Prefer pre-built toolchains over local source compilation. Run:

  wb-tools-manager.py check          # see what's available
  wb-tools-manager.py install mingw-w64-gcc   # download + verify + extract
  wb-tools-manager.py install glslang

Artifacts land under ~/.local/share/wine-bleeding/build-tools/<tool>/<version>/.
The manager is also available through wb-gui's preflight dialog ("Install via
manager" + "Check for updates" buttons).
